    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To file a roof insurance claim in Utah, contact your insurance company's claims center with your policy number and date of loss after documenting the damage and reviewing your deductible."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Review the essential step-by-step process below to navigate a roof claim efficiently in Utah:"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "1. Inspect and Document the Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Check for storm evidence: Look for hail impacts, missing or creased shingles from high winds, or leaks. Note the specific date the storm or weather event occurred (the date of loss)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Take photos and video: Capture wide-angle and close-up photos of damaged roof areas, as well as any interior water stains or ceiling peeling."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get a professional evaluation: Consider having a reputable local roofing contractor perform a free initial inspection to build a photo-backed report before calling your insurer."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "2. Review Your Policy and Deductible"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Check your declarations page for your specific wind and hail deductibles. Utah policies frequently use separate, percentage-based deductibles for wind and hail events rather than a standard flat fee."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Confirm whether your policy pays out on a Replacement Cost Value (RCV) or Actual Cash Value (ACV) basis."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "3. Prevent Further Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Take reasonable, temporary steps (like placing a tarp over a leaking section) to protect your home from additional harm."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Save all receipts for emergency materials, as these temporary costs are typically reimbursable under your policy. Do not make permanent repairs before your insurer inspects."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "4. File the Claim"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Call your insurance carrier's main claims line (rather than your local agent) to officially open the claim."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Provide the exact date of loss, the type of weather event (hail, wind, heavy snow), and your preliminary documentation."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Record your assigned claim number for all future communications."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "5. Meet the Insurance Adjuster"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Your insurer will assign an adjuster to inspect the roof."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ask your chosen roofing contractor to be present during the adjuster's inspection to ensure all storm damage is properly noted and nothing gets overlooked ."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "6. Review the Settlement and Begin Repairs"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Review the scope of work and estimate provided by your insurance company."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "If approved, the insurer will typically issue an initial ACV check to help you start work, releasing the remaining funds after repairs are completed and verified . You will be responsible for paying your out-of-pocket deductible directly to the contractor."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "For official guidelines and consumer assistance, refer to the Utah Insurance Department Home Claims Information .",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Utah Insurance Department Home Claims Information",
            "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
